BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Asheville Middle School
X-SOURCE-URL:https://ams.ashevillecityschools.net/asheville-middle-calendar
DTSTAMP:20260720T040341Z
UID:ee38e053-e5d4-51ce-a04c-3975f3a49e5c
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260118T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260118T230000
DESCRIPTION:Coverfest is back for its fifth spectacular year! Coverfest 
 V: A Benefit for Asheville Middle School will take over the Grey Eagle on 
 Sunday\, January 18\, 2026\, from 5:00-11:00 PM\, bringing together top l
 ocal and regional musicians for an unforgettable evening of cover songs.
  Over the past several years\, Coverfest has become a beloved fixture in
  Asheville's music scene\, raising money to ensure that every 8th grader c
 an participate in the annual capstone trip to Washington DC. We are so exc
 ited that this year will even feature a student band!"This trip is one of 
 the most important experiences our students will have during their middle 
 school years\," said Joe Hooten\, organizer\, performer\, and ACS teacher.
  "Our staff has vowed to not let any child stay behind due to their financ
 ial situation. This community's support ensures that promise becomes a rea
 lity." This year\, your support carries extra weight. With many families 
 still recovering from Hurricane Helene and new financial pressures due to 
 cuts in benefits\, our community's generosity is vital. Let’s pack The G
 rey Eagle and guarantee this essential educational experience for all 8th 
 graders!Tickets are available online through The Grey Eagle's website an
 d at the door on the night of the event. All proceeds go directly to fundi
 ng Asheville Middle School's 8th grade capstone trip\, ensuring every stud
 ent can benefit from this incredible learning experience.
LOCATION:The Grey Eagle Music Hall and Pub\, 185 Clingman Ave\, Asheville\,
  NC 28801\, USA
SUMMARY:Coverfest V - Washington DC Concert Fundraiser
END:VEVENT
